## 🎉 Rotating Card – Hover‑to‑Rotate (CSS Only)

Below is a **complete, ready‑to‑copy** example that shows a card with a front and back side.  
When you hover over the card, it flips (rotates) around the Y‑axis, revealing the back side.

> **Tip:**  
> - If you want a *vertical* flip, change `rotateY` → `rotateX`.  
> - For a *full 360°* rotation, use `rotateY(360deg)` (or `rotateX(360deg)`).

---

### 📄 HTML

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-face card-front">
      <h2>Front Side</h2>
      <p>Hover to flip!</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-face card-back">
      <h2>Back Side</h2>
      <p>Here’s the hidden content.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

---

### 🎨 CSS (`style.css`)

```css
/* 1️⃣  Global reset (optional but handy) */
*,
*::before,
*::after {
  box-sizing: border-box;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
}

/* 2️⃣  Center the card on the page */
body {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  min-height: 100vh;
  background: #f0f0f0;
  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
}

/* 3️⃣  Wrapper gives perspective for 3D effect */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* How far the viewer is from the card */
}

/* 4️⃣  The card itself */
.card {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;  /* Keep children in 3D space */
  transition: transform 0.8s ease; /* Smooth flip */
}

/* 5️⃣  Hover triggers the flip */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);   /* Rotate 180° around Y axis */
}

/* 6️⃣  Common styles for both faces */
.card-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden; /* Hide the back side when facing away */
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  color: #fff;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  text-align: center;
  padding: 20px;
  border-radius: 10px;
}

/* 7️⃣  Front side styling */
.card-front {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff6b6b, #f06595);
}

/* 8️⃣  Back side styling */
.card-back {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4a90e2, #357ab7);
  transform: rotateY(180deg);   /* Flip it so it starts hidden */
}

/* 9️⃣  Optional: Add a subtle shadow for depth */
.card {
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
}
```

---

### 🔍 How It Works

| Step | What Happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| 1 | Reset margins/padding | Keeps layout predictable |
| 2 | Center the card | Makes demo look nice |
| 3 | `perspective` on wrapper | Gives 3D depth perception |
| 4 | `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Keeps child elements in 3D space |
| 5 | `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the back side when it's turned away |
| 6 | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on hover | Flips the card |
| 7 | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on back face | Positions back side behind front |

---

### 📦 Quick Deployment

1. Create a folder (e.g., `rotating-card-demo`).
2. Inside, create `index.html` and paste the HTML above.
3. Create `style.css` and paste the CSS above.
4. Open `index.html` in a browser → Hover over the card to see the flip!

---

### 🎯 Customization Ideas

| Feature | How to Change |
|---------|---------------|
| **Card size** | Edit `.card` width/height |
| **Colors** | Replace gradients in `.card-front` / `.card-back` |
| **Animation speed** | Adjust `transition: transform 0.8s ease` |
| **Flip direction** | Use `rotateX` instead of `rotateY` |
| **Add more content** | Insert images, icons, or even nested cards |

---

